body:
Every \`[ ... ]\` keyword list in the grammar now parses against the declaration's own keywords: one \`#[derive(Grammar)]\` enum per kind (class, method, property, parameter, index, query, trigger, foreign key, XData, projection) listing all 139 keywords of the class definition reference, with \`Flag<Name>\` for a flag (\`X\`, \`Not X\`) and \`Valued<Name, Shape>\` for a value. A value the checker reads has its own shape (\`ClassType\`, \`Inheritance\`, \`Cardinality\`, \`IndexType\`, \`CodeMode\`, \`MethodLanguage\`, \`ClassList\`, the \`Bit\` of \`ProcedureBlock = 0\`); any other is taken as written. The keywords every member takes, \`Deprecated\` and \`Internal\`, are one nested \`MemberKeyword\` list.

An entry that is none of them falls back to the generic entry (\`FailableKeyword<K> = Either<K, KeywordEntry>\`), so IRIS's own exports still parse whole, and the checker reports it:

\`\`\`objectscript
Class Demo.Keywords Extends %Persistent [ Bogus, ClassType = Persistent, Inheritance = middle, Abstract = 0 ]
{
Property P As %String [ Aliases, Cardinality = few ];
Index I On P [ Type = banana ];
ClassMethod M() [ Language = cobol, Abstract = 1 ]
{
}
}
\`\`\`

IRIS compiles past a class keyword it can't place, dropping it or, for a flag, taking it as the bare flag (\`Abstract = 0\` compiles abstract), except \`ClassType\` (ERROR #7852); a member keyword it can't place fails the class (ERROR #5559), \`Abstract = 1\` included, since a member's flag takes no value:

\`\`\`
wa

Added a `Triage` workflow:
- assigns every new issue to @isc-klu;
- requests @isc-bsaviano's review on every PR once ready (not on his own)
